course: dictionary
lesson: 5503
title: One word, many layers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and layer is one of them. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants. Read the words around it: «Penguins also keep warm with a thick layer of fat and tightly packed waterproof feathers.» Here a layer is a thick covering under the skin, so it means a covering over something.
explain: Layer can also be a verb, meaning to put things in layers. Dad says, «Layer your clothes when it is cold.» He does not mean a single layer of clothes; he means put several thin clothes on top of each other to keep warm.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «A graze scrapes off the top layer of skin» still makes sense if you read layer as a thin covering over the skin, so that is the right meaning.
fact: A layer is one flat level of something lying on top of or under another, like a layer of a cake.
fact: A layer can be a thin covering over a surface, like «a layer of dust» or «a layer of paint».
fact: To layer means to put things in layers, like layering clothes in cold weather.
fact: A layer can also be a hen that lays eggs. Use the context to tell which meaning is which.
exercise: «Where hands rub a brass door knob or a statue's nose every day, the thin dull layer is rubbed off.» What is the layer in this sentence? | A flat level inside a cake | A set of steps up to the statue | A hen that lays eggs | *A thin covering over the metal
exercise: Which sentence uses layer to mean a hen that lays eggs? | «The top layer of the cake is chocolate.» | *«The farm's best layer gave two eggs today.» | «Wear a layer of warm clothes on a cold day.» | «A thick layer of snow covered the field.»
exercise: Dad says, «Layer your clothes when it is cold.» What should you do? | Take all your clothes off | Wash your clothes in cold water | *Put on several thin clothes, one over another | Buy one very thick coat and nothing else
test: The Earth has layers. Which of these is the outermost layer of the Earth? | Ocean | Core | *Crust | Mantle
test: «Salt is spread on icy roads because salty water freezes at a lower temperature; the salt dissolves in the thin wet layer on the ice.» What does layer mean here? | *A thin covering on the ice | A stack of bricks | A hen that lays eggs | A sheet of paper
exam: Which sentence uses layer as a verb, meaning to put things in layers? | «Skin has a top layer.» | «The ozone layer is high up in the sky.» | *«On cold days, layer a vest under your jumper.» | «A hen is a layer.»
